Here's a little thing to help make pools more distinguishable from
fountains.  It doesn't solve the whole problem of pools; it's just
something that might be helpful until nethack starts confirming
pool dives (or decides not to).

I set the 'pool' graphic to be '8' in the NETHACKOPTIONS environment
variable.  It's a pretty distinctive symbol I think.  Of course you
can change it to anything you like.

Here's how it looks in my .cshrc:

setenv NETHACKOPTIONS 'graphics: |--------|||-\\/.-|+.#<>\^"8{#\\_<>##'
Ugly, huh?  :-) Anyway, whatever character you put there where the '8' is will
be displayed for pools.

Other shells may need more backslashes.  For instance bash takes:
export NETHACKOPTIONS='graphics: |--------|||-\\\\/.-|+.#<>\\^"8{#\\\\\_<>##'
I don't know why it needs a clump of five!  That just seems to work.

Hope this helps, and happy hacking,
